Time complexity = measure of how efficient the algorithm is in terms of speed and space it takes.

1. o(1)
2. o(log n)
3. o(n)
4. o(n log n)
5. o(n^2)
6. o(2^n)
7. o(n!)


Space complexity - if we use any extra space

1. o(1)
2. o(n)

if we have more time complexities like (o(n^2 + nlogn + 2n)) -> in this case we consider the bigger one and 
neglect the rest so it boils down to o(n^2)